    "body": "# Nightly guide refresh\n\nRefreshed: 2026-09-26T20:59:09.544444+00:00\n\nSaved GitHub data and generated guide only. This PR does not merge or publish the guide.\n\n## agent-device-hub\n\n- Closed: H278 — Reach every B.U.N.N.Y. surface from one shared places navigation\n- Relabelled: H278 — documentation, enhancement, status:backlog → documentation, enhancement\n- Closed: H315 — Refresh the work guide nightly into one rolling pull request\n- Retitled: H427 — Document upgrading the installed hub with a backup, receipt and rollback → Upgrade and roll back the installed hub with one command under the install contract\n- Relabelled: H427 — documentation, status:backlog → blocked, documentation, status:backlog\n- Relabelled: H428 — enhancement, status:backlog → blocked, enhancement, status:backlog\n- Opened: H465 — Define the shared install contract and receipt schema for installed runtimes\n- Opened: H467 — Plan Wispr analytics: local collection, private dashboard and future speaking insights\n- Opened: H468 — Collect Wispr usage locally on Windows and publish private aggregate snapshots\n- Opened: H469 — Add opt-in Wispr word, phrase and text-change aggregates\n- Opened: H470 — Serve private Wispr aggregates through source-authorized hub routes\n- Opened: H471 — Show Wispr usage, phrase and correction trends in the B.U.N.N.Y. dashboard\n- Opened: H472 — Install and verify the private Wispr collector and dashboard on the owner PC\n- Opened: H473 — Explore personal speaking-improvement goals from Wispr trends\n- Opened: H474 — Explore reviewed Wispr dictionary and snippet suggestions from repeated edits\n- Opened: H475 — Investigate Wispr mobile usage exports and optional iPhone Shortcut capture\n- Opened: H476 — Finish owned local branch and worktree cleanup with a verified outcome\n- Opened: H477 — Review and clean the accumulated local delivery artifacts\n- Opened: H478 — Capture song plays, skips and metadata for private B.U.N.N.Y. music widgets\n- Opened: H479 — Define evidence-backed agent delivery effectiveness measures\n- Opened: H480 — Qualify Codex and Claude usage sources for private B.U.N.N.Y. widgets\n- Opened: H481 — Qualify PlayStation, Xbox and Nintendo game data sources for B.U.N.N.Y.\n- Opened: H482 — Qualify read-only Robinhood data sources for B.U.N.N.Y.\n- Opened: H483 — Add two Wemo Mini F7C063 plugs to B.U.N.N.Y. after local qualification\n- Opened: H484 — Qualify Galaxy Lamps GPUS projector integration\n- Opened: H485 — Qualify BlissLights Sky Lite 2.0 Bluetooth integration\n\nTopic counts (open stories):\n\n- assistant-access: 26 → 26\n- bunny-controls: 27 → 38\n- controls-music: 16 → 17\n- desktop-controls: 12 → 12\n- development-workflow: 8 → 10\n- hosting-migrations: 8 → 9\n- nanoleaf-devices: 22 → 25\n- pixoo-media: 3 → 3\n- shared-codex: 21 → 22\n- steam-deck: 8 → 9\n- work-guide: 19 → 17\n\nRecommendation state changes:\n\n- H356 — stale → recommended\n- H428 — insufficient → recommended\n- H459 — unavailable → insufficient\n- H465 — absent → recommended\n- H467 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H468 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H469 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H470 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H471 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H472 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H473 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H474 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H475 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H476 — absent → recommended\n- H477 — absent → recommended\n- H478 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H479 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H480 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H481 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H482 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H483 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H484 — absent → not yet assessed\n- H485 — absent → not yet assessed\n\n## codex-nanoleaf\n\n- Retitled: N140 — Add an upgrade and rollback command for the Linux runtime → Upgrade and roll back the Linux runtime with one command under the install contract\n- Relabelled: N140 — maintenance, status:backlog → blocked, maintenance, status:backlog\n- Retitled: N162 — Document the in-place runtime upgrade, the codex exec MCP override and the hand-listed bridge modules → Document the codex exec MCP override and the hand-listed bridge modules\n- Closed: N179 — Use shared session titles and project names instead of local-only metadata\n- Opened: N192 — Finish owned local branch and worktree cleanup with a verified outcome\n\nTopic counts (open stories):\n\n- assistant-access: 2 → 2\n- development-workflow: 9 → 10\n- hosting-migrations: 2 → 2\n- nanoleaf-devices: 8 → 7\n- nanoleaf-presentation: 19 → 19\n- shared-codex: 3 → 3\n\nRecommendation state changes:\n\n- N162 — stale → recommended\n- N192 — absent → recommended\n\n## divoom-app-upgrade\n\n- Relabelled: P114 — enhancement, status:backlog → blocked, enhancement, status:backlog\n- Opened: P115 — Upgrade and roll back the Pixoo user service with one command under the install contract\n- Opened: P117 — Finish owned local branch and worktree cleanup with a verified outcome\n\nTopic counts (open stories):\n\n- assistant-access: 4 → 4\n- development-workflow: 2 → 3\n- hosting-migrations: 3 → 4\n- pixoo-media: 13 → 13\n- shared-codex: 4 → 4\n\nRecommendation state changes:\n\n- P114 — insufficient → recommended\n- P115 — absent → recommended\n- P117 — absent → recommended\n\n## Direction check: passed\n\nThe existing Direction checks passed; the narrative remains owner-written.\n\n## Retired-term warnings\n\n- H36: story cites retired term PowerShell (retired by N131)\n- N121: story cites retired term PowerShell (retired by N131)\n- N123: story cites retired term install-modes.ps1 (retired by N131)\n\nSource: `55f11cb0b785e2123711b3e8720489205c02dec4`. Mode: `live`. Baseline maintenance passed before refresh.\n\nFresh generation, deterministic rebuild, maintenance and browser checks passed.\n",
